          '**Pre-Operative Medical Optimization** (5 days available):\n\n1. **Infection Control**:\n- Continue IV antibiotics; obtain wound cultures to guide therapy\n- Monitor WBC, ESR, CRP trends\n- Ensure no ascending osteomyelitis above the planned amputation level (MRI or bone scan if concerned)\n\n2. **Glycemic Control**:\n- HbA1c 9.2% reflects chronic poor control; perioperative hyperglycemia increases surgical site infection risk\n- Target blood glucose 140-180 mg/dL perioperatively (avoid tight control <110 due to hypoglycemia risk)\n- May need insulin drip perioperatively; adjust basal/bolus regimen\n- Endocrinology consultation for long-term diabetes management optimization\n\n3. **Cardiac Risk Assessment**:\n- History of CABG and CAD — assess functional capacity. If <4 METs, consider cardiology clearance.\n- ECG, echocardiogram if not recent. Optimize medical therapy (continue aspirin, statin, ACE inhibitor).\n- BKA is a moderate-risk surgical procedure. Revised Cardiac Risk Index (RCRI) assessment.\n\n4. **Pulmonary Optimization**:\n- COPD with SpO2 94% at baseline — pulmonary function should be optimized pre-operatively\n- Incentive spirometry teaching pre-operatively\n- Albuterol nebulizer treatments PRN perioperatively\n- Smoking cessation confirmed (quit 5 years ago — good)\n\n5. **Nutritional Optimization**:\n- Albumin 3.0 and prealbumin 14 are both low — associated with poor wound healing\n- Start high-protein oral supplementation immediately (1.5-2.0 g/kg/day protein)\n- Caloric goal: 30-35 kcal/kg/day\n- Vitamin C 500 mg BID and zinc 220 mg daily for wound healing\n- Dietitian consultation urgently\n\n6. **Renal Considerations**:\n- CKD Stage 3a — adjust medications for renal function\n- Avoid nephrotoxic agents; ensure adequate hydration perioperatively\n- Monitor electrolytes closely given diabetes and CKD\n\n7. **Mental Health**:\n- Depression screening (he reports feeling "useless") — PHQ-9 baseline\n- Ensure sertraline dose is optimized\n- Pre-operative counseling about what to expect post-surgically\n- Consider psychology referral for pre-amputation counseling\n\n8. **Pre-Amputation Rehabilitation** (Prehabilitation):\n- Upper extremity strengthening for walker/crutch use post-operatively\n- Core strengthening\n- Single-leg balance training on the left leg (carefully, given neuropathy)\n- Wheelchair training for immediate post-operative mobility\n- Home accessibility assessment and equipment ordering (wheelchair, shower bench, grab bars)',
